      "Projectiles": {
        "VoyageHazard": {
          "DisplayName": "Star-Sea Combat Energy"
        }
      },
      "VoyageBestiary": {
        "StarportSovereign": "A derelict freight port still operates inside its gel. Destroy cargo before it opens. Low-gravity pockets alter falling but deal no damage.",
        "Farwatcher": "It remembers your recent path, not your next decision. Faint traces record the route; bright beams are the actual shots.",
        "BeltDevourer": "Nine independently damageable sections share one fixed encounter budget. Breaking middle sections forms a second short body without adding health.",
        "ConsensusBrain": "Neural satellites relay attacks in order. Breaking a node cancels its attacks and staggers the brain. Disconnected decoys have no hitbox.",
        "HiveCarrier": "Two destructible hangars launch bounded drone formations. Destroy them to stop reinforcements and force the carrier to use its own cannon.",
        "OrbitalAnchor": "Two docking anchors define the chains. Breaking one staggers the marshal. Watch which cable it begins to retrieve.",
        "WarpBulwark": "The advancing living bulkhead always leaves a traversable lane. There is no solid contact wall, and no attack changes player-built tiles.",
        "CrystalOrbitQueen": "Three breakable crystals define the reflected paths. Every segment is shown before firing; a broken crystal opens a route.",
        "BinaryHunters": "Redshift intercepts while Blueshift covers. Each eye owns half the total budget. The survivor inherits one reduced tactic, never extra life.",
        "FourArmTribunal": "Four non-respawning weapon arms are scheduled two at a time. Dismantle difficult weapons while the central chassis remains vulnerable.",
        "SunpiercerFleet": "The bow and eight ship sections have separate budgets. Breaking cooling sections two or five slows the train; detached escorts add no health.",
        "Worldseed": "Four root nodes connect temporary routes. Breaking a node opens space, and seeds never turn into permanent world tiles.",
        "PrecursorGuardian": "Precursor blocks rearrange between attacks, then activate their geometric stamps in sequence. Breaking a block creates a recovery opening.",
        "AetherLeviathan": "It hunts along committed flight paths. Wakes become dangerous after a delay; the later inhale clears old wakes for another hunt.",
        "SolarSailEmpress": "The optical film carries the light, but the path is what matters. Destroy sails to simplify reflection. Daytime never adds an instant-kill rule.",
        "StarNavigator": "Real gates fire in coordinate order; hollow disconnected beacons are illusions. Breaking a real gate disrupts the ritual and staggers its navigator.",
        "CelestialArk": "Left city: 2 million. Right city: 2 million. Array: 2.5 million. Core: 3.5 million. Exactly ten million before difficulty scaling; the final voyage previews a curved safe route."
      },
